From 6e4be7a0df1bc27963b36f47f0bd5d1a59c6d560 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: c4ffein <c4ffein.work@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 20:54:35 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 234/248] Bugfix: accept deprecated strategy parameters in
 strategy value check

The check added to the nested-strategy alternative of PARAMVAL compared
the parameter type with STRATPARAMSTRAT without masking
STRATPARAMDEPRECATED, unlike the lookup done a few lines above, which
uses 'typeval & ~STRATPARAMDEPRECATED'. A deprecated parameter that
takes a strategy would hence have its value rejected instead of being
parsed and ignored, as is done for deprecated scalar parameters. No
such parameter exists in the current tables, so the defect is latent.

Tested with a throw-away tree where bgraph method 'm', parameter 'asc',
was declared 'STRATPARAMDEPRECATED | STRATPARAMSTRAT': strategy
'r{sep=m{asc=f}}' gave 'invalid value for parameter asc' before and
ret=0 after; 'm{vert=()}' is still rejected.
---
 src/libscotch/parser_yy.y | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/libscotch/parser_yy.y b/src/libscotch/parser_yy.y
index d7ed163..2588617 100644
--- a/src/libscotch/parser_yy.y
+++ b/src/libscotch/parser_yy.y
@@ -469,7 +469,7 @@ PARAMVAL      : VALCASE
               }
               | <SAVE>
               {
-                if (penvptr->paraptr->typeval != STRATPARAMSTRAT) /* If parameter cannot hold a strategy */
+                if ((penvptr->paraptr->typeval & ~STRATPARAMDEPRECATED) != STRATPARAMSTRAT) /* If parameter cannot hold a strategy */
                   YYERROR;                        /* Report invalid parameter value         */
 
                 ($$).strat = penvptr->straptr;    /* Save current method and parameter; typed value is restored by destructor on error */
